MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The direction/packing pages now show which state the served day is in, and a
not-yet-issued day explains itself instead of rendering a blank table — the exact
confusion the maintainer flagged (defaulting to tomorrow, which is pending, showed
an empty grid with no reason).

Shared FeedLifecycleBanner (mock .alert anatomy + .tag chips, lucide, var(--*)):
- issued  — "Issued <at>"
- amended — "Amended <at> · N correction(s)"
- locked  — "Locked <at> — transport has left; changes roll to the next feed day"
- pending — "Not issued yet <day>" + per-workflow expected issue times; this
            REPLACES the empty table (banner is the content), guarded so a filter
            that merely excludes rows still shows the normal "no rows match" state
- not_issued — "No sheet was issued for <day>" (the issue time passed, honest gap)
- draft   — "DRAFT — live preview, not an issued sheet"

Mixed per-workflow states are legible (normal issued 07:00 while experiment still
pending till 14:00); aggregate state is the least-advanced, but the hide-table
decision keys off row count so a partially-issued day still renders its rows.

All labels are backend copy (service.go pageSpecificCopy, both feed cases);
dates are client-formatted in Asia/Kolkata after the copy labels. Rendering only —
no lifecycle semantics changed.

Gap noted, not invented: the row contract exposes no per-row `amended` flag, so
individual corrected rows aren't badged yet; sheet-level amendment_count is shown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
